2) FengWu paper
---------------
Chen et al., "FengWu: Pushing the Skillful Global Medium-range Weather
Forecast beyond 10 Days Lead", arXiv:2304.02948
https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.02948

The `FengWu` / `FengWu_lite` modules are a clean WeatherLearn-style
reimplementation inspired by the paper architecture (encode–fuse–decode,
optional uncertainty head). They do **not** vendor proprietary training
configs or non-MIT checkpoints.

3) GraphCast paper
------------------
Lam et al., "GraphCast: Learning skillful medium-range global weather
forecasting", Science 2023 / arXiv:2212.12794
https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.12794

The `GraphCast` / `GraphCast_lite` modules are an independent WeatherAI-style
PyTorch reimplementation (lat-lon grid ↔ icosahedral multi-mesh
encode–process–decode with residual next-step prediction). They do **not**
copy source from google-deepmind/graphcast or NVIDIA PhysicsNeMo (Apache-2.0).
See `docs/graphcast_specs.md` for paper vs skeleton differences.

