5) DeepMind GraphCast / WeatherNext (Apache-2.0) — reference only
----------------------------------------------------------------
Source: https://github.com/google-deepmind/graphcast
Copyright (c) Google LLC / DeepMind Technologies Limited

WeatherAI’s `weatherai.models.graphcast` package is an **independent MIT**
PyTorch reimplementation. It does **not** copy or relicense DeepMind sources
as MIT.

For **parity tests** only, developers may clone the official repository
(e.g. under `/workspace/tmp/graphcast-jax`) and import JAX modules from that
tree. Those Apache-2.0 files stay outside the `weatherai/` package. See
`docs/graphcast_parity.md` and `tests/parity/graphcast/`.

Mesh geometry (icosahedron face index table / refinement order) is aligned with
the published helpers for interoperability; that is geometric compatibility, not
a vendored copy of their Python modules.

Package rename
--------------
Imports use the package name `weatherai` (not `weatherlearn`). Relative module
layout mirrors WeatherLearn-style `models/{pangu,fuxi,fengwu,graphcast}` for
familiarity.
